load @term/seed/code/structure/manifold
  find manifold

# The hyperbolic plane, the two-dimensional space of constant negative curvature, the third geometry beside the sphere
# and the flat plane, and the home of everything the substrate's bulk is modelled on. It is the unique (up to scale)
# simply-connected complete surface of constant negative curvature, and its defining features all flow from the
# hyperbolic parallel axiom (see the axiom file).

# The plane itself: a complete, simply-connected, homogeneous, isotropic surface of constant negative Gaussian
# curvature. Homogeneous and isotropic mean it looks the same from every point and in every direction, so it has a rich
# symmetry group (the isometries form a three-dimensional Lie group). The form carries the underlying manifold.
form hyperbolic-plane
  link manifold, like manifold

# Thin triangles: every triangle has angle sum below two right angles, and the deficit equals the area. There are no
# similar-but-unequal triangles (AAA congruence) and no rectangles. As a triangle's vertices recede to infinity its
# angles shrink to zero and its area approaches the maximal ideal-triangle area. The form carries the plane.
form thin-triangle
  link plane, like hyperbolic-plane

# Exponential measure: a circle of radius r has circumference proportional to the hyperbolic sine of r and area to the
# hyperbolic cosine of r minus one, both growing exponentially, against the linear circumference and quadratic area of
# the flat plane. Most of the plane is "near the edge": almost all of a large disk's area lies in a thin outer shell.
# The form carries the plane.
form exponential-measure
  link plane, like hyperbolic-plane

# The isometry group: the distance-preserving maps of the hyperbolic plane are the projective special linear group of
# two-by-two real matrices (orientation-preserving) extended by reflections, acting on the boundary circle by Mobius
# transformations. It is generated by reflections in geodesics, the Coxeter-group fact that makes the tilings. The form
# carries the plane whose symmetries these are.
form hyperbolic-isometry-group
  link plane, like hyperbolic-plane
